      "back": "Judging likelihood by how easily examples come to mind — recent/vivid events overweighted",
      "tags": [
        "heuristic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "front": "Anchoring",
      "back": "Over-relying on the first piece of information encountered when making estimates",
      "tags": [
        "heuristic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "front": "Dunning-Kruger effect",
      "back": "Low-competence people overestimate ability; experts underestimate — inverse U of confidence",
      "tags": [
        "metacognition"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "front": "Sunk cost fallacy",
      "back": "Continuing a course of action because of past unrecoverable investment",
